{
  "apiVersion": "edge.forms.takoform.com",
  "kind": "ContainerService",
  "definitionVersion": "0.1.0-dev.1",
  "title": "Container Service",
  "description": "Unpublished Edge install-owned Container Service candidate. It runs one application-selected OCI image identified by a SHA-256 digest and exposes one application HTTP port after the required health path succeeds. image, port, healthPath, environment, requiredSensitiveVars, workloadRevision, and outboundInternet are application intent; provider, registry credential, native IDs, capacity, filesystem, endpoint, and secret values remain outside portable state. Lifecycle is create, read, update, observe, and delete; import is not claimed and no portable outputs are declared. workloadRevision is an application-owned non-secret revision token: changing it deliberately starts a new execution generation and is required for secret-only rotation, while secret bytes arrive through a separate sealed input and never enter the Form. The host starts a new revision before cutover; an unhealthy new generation does not replace the old serving generation, and the old generation may remain Ready while that update is unhealthy. servingGeneration is observed only as a canonical positive-decimal string when selection exists. outboundInternet=true grants isolated outbound Internet and DNS only: it does not grant host networking, metadata access, private sibling access, or inbound publication; a host unable to enforce this isolation refuses the resource. This candidate introduces no Actor, WebSocket, or new stable contract and requires the Host/Provider to reject any environment/requiredSensitiveVars name overlap at instance admission (released Core's closed constraint vocabulary cannot express that cross-list relation). It does not imply a separate family, new namespace, Host support, admission, or publication. Secret-bearing workload support additionally requires a concrete generation-bound sealed-input adapter, which this publisher candidate does not implement.",
  "role": "identity",
  "requiresHostApi": "forms.takoform.com/v1",
  "constraints": [
    {
      "kind": "uniqueBy",
      "list": "/environment",
      "member": "name"
    }
  ],
  "desiredSchema": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "description": "Unpublished Edge install-owned Container Service candidate. It runs one application-selected OCI image identified by a SHA-256 digest and exposes one application HTTP port after the required health path succeeds. image, port, healthPath, environment, requiredSensitiveVars, workloadRevision, and outboundInternet are application intent; provider, registry credential, native IDs, capacity, filesystem, endpoint, and secret values remain outside portable state. Lifecycle is create, read, update, observe, and delete; import is not claimed and no portable outputs are declared. workloadRevision is an application-owned non-secret revision token: changing it deliberately starts a new execution generation and is required for secret-only rotation, while secret bytes arrive through a separate sealed input and never enter the Form. The host starts a new revision before cutover; an unhealthy new generation does not replace the old serving generation, and the old generation may remain Ready while that update is unhealthy. servingGeneration is observed only as a canonical positive-decimal string when selection exists. outboundInternet=true grants isolated outbound Internet and DNS only: it does not grant host networking, metadata access, private sibling access, or inbound publication; a host unable to enforce this isolation refuses the resource. This candidate introduces no Actor, WebSocket, or new stable contract and requires the Host/Provider to reject any environment/requiredSensitiveVars name overlap at instance admission (released Core's closed constraint vocabulary cannot express that cross-list relation). It does not imply a separate family, new namespace, Host support, admission, or publication. Secret-bearing workload support additionally requires a concrete generation-bound sealed-input adapter, which this publisher candidate does not implement.",
    "properties": {
      "environment": {
        "default": [],
        "description": "Optional non-secret application environment entries. Each entry has a unique ASCII name matching ^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}$ and a bounded value without NUL; omission means []. Names must be disjoint from requiredSensitiveVars before mutation.",
        "items": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "name": {
              "description": "ASCII environment identifier; entries are unique by name.",
              "maxLength": 128,
              "pattern": "^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}$",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "value": {
              "description": "Non-secret environment value without NUL.",
              "maxLength": 8192,
              "pattern": "^[^\\x00]*$",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "name",
            "value"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "maxItems": 128,
        "type": "array",
        "uniqueItems": true
      },
      "healthPath": {
        "description": "Required absolute HTTP path checked with GET before a generation is eligible to serve. It has one leading slash, no authority/URL form, fragment, backslash, whitespace, or control character; the host never treats it as a public endpoint.",
        "maxLength": 1024,
        "pattern": "^/([^/\\\\#\\x00-\\x20\\x7F-\\x9F][^\\\\#\\x00-\\x20\\x7F-\\x9F]*|)$",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "image": {
        "description": "Required OCI image reference pinned to one lowercase sha256 digest (name@sha256:<64 lowercase hex digits>). Repository components use the lowercase distribution/reference subset [a-z0-9]+ with [._], __, or hyphen separators; an optional lowercase DNS/IPv4/localhost registry prefix and port 1..65535 may appear only before a slash. Mutable tags, tag-only references, IPv6 literals, userinfo, registry credentials, and native image IDs are outside this first candidate; a host resolves the exact digest before starting the revision.",
        "maxLength": 512,
        "pattern": "^(?:(?:localhost|(?:[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]*[a-z0-9])?\\.)*[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]*[a-z0-9])?|(?:(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|[1-9]?[0-9])\\.){3}(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|[1-9]?[0-9]))(?::(?:[1-9][0-9]{0,3}|[1-5][0-9]{4}|6[0-4][0-9]{3}|65[0-4][0-9]{2}|655[0-2][0-9]|6553[0-5]))?/)?[a-z0-9]+(?:(?:[._]|__|-+)[a-z0-9]+)*(?:/[a-z0-9]+(?:(?:[._]|__|-+)[a-z0-9]+)*)*@sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "outboundInternet": {
        "default": false,
        "description": "Whether the isolated process may make outbound Internet and DNS requests. The default false denies egress; true never grants host networking, metadata/private sibling access, inbound exposure, or provider credentials, and a Host unable to enforce those boundaries refuses the resource.",
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "port": {
        "description": "Required application HTTP port in the inclusive range 1..65535. The host connects to the isolated process on this port; it is not a host listener or a public endpoint.",
        "maximum": 65535,
        "minimum": 1,
        "type": "integer"
      },
      "requiredSensitiveVars": {
        "default": [],
        "description": "Optional unique set of ASCII environment names whose values the host must provide through a separate generation-bound sealed input. Only names are portable; values never appear in desired, observed, output, logs, or diagnostics. Omission means no required sensitive values, and names must be disjoint from environment.",
        "items": {
          "pattern": "^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}$",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "maxItems": 64,
        "type": "array",
        "uniqueItems": true
      },
      "workloadRevision": {
        "description": "Required application-owned non-secret revision token. It is not a provider nonce, operation key, native identity, or secret-derived value. Changing it is the explicit portable signal for a new execution generation, including a secret-only rotation; an old revision is never mutated under the same serving generation.",
        "maxLength": 64,
        "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$",
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "healthPath",
      "image",
      "port",
      "workloadRevision"
    ],
    "title": "Container Service desired state",
    "type": "object"
  },
  "observedSchema": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "description": "Observed serving selection only. An empty object is the valid pre-cutover state; this schema carries no provider/native identity and makes no application data consistency claim.",
    "properties": {
      "servingGeneration": {
        "description": "Canonical positive decimal generation, 1..9223372036854775807. It is absent before the first serving selection and is a string rather than a JSON number.",
        "maxLength": 19,
        "pattern": "^(?:[1-9][0-9]{0,17}|[1-8][0-9]{18}|9[0-1][0-9]{17}|92[0-1][0-9]{16}|922[0-2][0-9]{15}|9223[0-2][0-9]{14}|92233[0-6][0-9]{13}|922337[0-1][0-9]{12}|92233720[0-2][0-9]{10}|922337203[0-5][0-9]{9}|9223372036[0-7][0-9]{8}|92233720368[0-4][0-9]{7}|922337203685[0-3][0-9]{6}|9223372036854[0-6][0-9]{5}|92233720368547[0-6][0-9]{4}|922337203685477[0-4][0-9]{3}|9223372036854775[0-7][0-9]{2}|922337203685477580[0-7])$",
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "type": "object"
  },
  "lifecycleCapabilities": [
    "create",
    "read",
    "update",
    "observe",
    "delete"
  ],
  "providedInterfaces": [
    {
      "apiVersion": "interfaces.takoform.com/v1alpha1",
      "name": "container.http",
      "version": "0.1.0",
      "schemaDigest": "sha256:65039b3ea0223057e5f34eff182098a1ba097ee351e19fcb7626a9af41a8561a"
    }
  ],
  "conformanceFixtures": [
    {
      "name": "canonical",
      "desiredPath": "fixtures/desired.json",
      "observedPath": "fixtures/observed-empty.json"
    }
  ],
  "negativeConformanceFixtures": [
    {
      "name": "reject-unexpected-property",
      "stage": "desired",
      "inputPath": "fixtures/negative-unexpected-property.json",
      "expectedFailure": "schema_validation_failed"
    },
    {
      "name": "reject-missing-image",
      "stage": "desired",
      "inputPath": "fixtures/negative-missing-image.json",
      "expectedFailure": "schema_validation_failed"
    },
    {
      "name": "reject-missing-port",
      "stage": "desired",
      "inputPath": "fixtures/negative-missing-port.json",
      "expectedFailure": "schema_validation_failed"
    },
    {
      "name": "reject-missing-health-path",
      "stage": "desired",
      "inputPath": "fixtures/negative-missing-health-path.json",
      "expectedFailure": "schema_validation_failed"
    },
    {
      "name": "reject-missing-workload-revision",
      "stage": "desired",
      "inputPath": "fixtures/negative-missing-workload-revision.json",
      "expectedFailure": "schema_validation_failed"
    },
    {
      "name": "reject-image",
      "stage": "desired",
      "inputPath": "fixtures/negative-image.json",
      "expectedFailure": "schema_validation_failed"
    },
    {
      "name": "reject-port",
      "stage": "desired",
      "inputPath": "fixtures/negative-port.json",
      "expectedFailure": "schema_validation_failed"
    },
    {
      "name": "reject-health-path",
      "stage": "desired",
      "inputPath": "fixtures/negative-health-path.json",
      "expectedFailure": "schema_validation_failed"
    },
    {
      "name": "reject-environment",
      "stage": "desired",
      "inputPath": "fixtures/negative-environment.json",
      "expectedFailure": "schema_validation_failed"
    },
    {
      "name": "reject-required-sensitive-vars",
      "stage": "desired",
      "inputPath": "fixtures/negative-required-sensitive-vars.json",
      "expectedFailure": "schema_validation_failed"
    },
    {
      "name": "reject-workload-revision",
      "stage": "desired",
      "inputPath": "fixtures/negative-workload-revision.json",
      "expectedFailure": "schema_validation_failed"
    }
  ]
}

interface.definitionJson:
{
  "apiVersion": "interfaces.takoform.com/v1alpha1",
  "kind": "InterfaceDefinition",
  "name": "container.http",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "title": "Container HTTP service invocation",
  "description": "Unpublished container.http candidate for invoking the HTTP surface of one logical ContainerService. The target is selected only by the authorized logical Resource UID and incarnation through the Binding; a URL host, native address, process ID, or provider identity never selects a target. The serving-selection consistency value is per_key_linearizable only for this exact service UID/incarnation and cutover selection; it makes no consistency claim about application data. Request and response bodies travel beside these documents as streams. bodyStream=false with contentLength=0 means ABSENT; bodyStream=true with contentLength=0 means PRESENT BUT EMPTY; bodyStream=true with contentLength=null means PRESENT WITH UNKNOWN LENGTH. A count is never invented or learned by buffering: an integer is an exact promise, and a mismatch is a stream error. Dispatch starts after the request head, before request bytes are consumed, and the Promise resolves at the response head, before response bytes are consumed. Backpressure and cancellation propagate in both directions. The candidate accepts at most 104857600 body bytes, 64 header entries, 16384 aggregate header bytes per direction, and an 8192-character origin-form path; these are exact candidate ceilings, not the worker.service Interface's portable floors. Within these Interface transport documents, header entries preserve order and repetition; names use HTTP token ASCII, values use HTAB/U+0020..U+007E/U+0080..U+00FF, and aggregate bytes are the Latin-1 length of name + 2 + value + 2 for every entry. Host and other transport hop-by-hop fields, including Connection-nominated names, are removed before forwarding, while application Authorization is preserved as end-to-end data and is separate from Host routing authority. Known oversize requests fail before dispatch; an unknown stream aborts once it crosses the limit and may have partially delivered bytes. Before a response head, backend_unavailable, request_aborted, request_too_large, response_too_large, and invalid_request reject the call with no synthetic HTTP status. After the head, response_aborted and response_too_large are errored response-body outcomes with the received status. Application 4xx/5xx statuses are normal responses, not JavaScript throws or synthetic 500s. There is no transparent retry after uncertain I/O; a response-header aggregate overflow before the response head is reported as backend_unavailable. Content-Length is not an application header: contentLength is the sole transport-document framing authority. The Binding extracts one canonical non-negative decimal Content-Length at its Fetch boundary and removes it from projected application headers; duplicate, comma-joined, conflicting, or invalid request framing is invalid_request before dispatch. Without a known exact request length, contentLength is null. A request count mismatch is request_aborted; after an early response head, abort the upload and any still-open response stream without replacing delivered status or bytes, or retrying. A response count mismatch aborts the exposed body as response_aborted. Native response Content-Length is validated and removed before projection; duplicate or invalid native framing is backend_unavailable before the head. A known response above 104857600 bytes is response_too_large before its head, and unknown overflow is the same body error after the head. The Binding projects standard Fetch Headers: arbitrary duplicate fields may combine and their order/casing are not promised, while Set-Cookie remains separately available through getSetCookie(). existing calls remain pinned through cutover and the declared 30000ms drain bound. HEAD, 204, 205, and 304 responses carry no body (HEAD's contentLength is 0 even if a representation header would have claimed another size). Every other non-HEAD response carries bodyStream=true, including a known zero-byte stream; HTTP does not preserve a server language's null-versus-empty response distinction.",
  "operations": [
    {
      "name": "fetch",
      "description": "Invoke one ContainerService HTTP request. Closed request and response documents carry method/path, optional ordered headers, body presence, and nullable exact contentLength; bytes stream beside them. GET and HEAD have no request body. The Promise resolves at response head. Pre-head failures are backend_unavailable, request_aborted, request_too_large, response_too_large, or invalid_request; post-head body failures are response_aborted or response_too_large. Declared count mismatches abort, unknown counts are never fabricated, and application errors resolve normally. Fixture service responses are GET /healthz 200 with a zero-byte stream, POST /echo 200 with ordered repeated Set-Cookie headers and zero-byte stream, GET /missing 404 with a zero-byte stream, and /close-before-head backend_unavailable; response-header overflow before its head is backend_unavailable. Fixtures are metadata-only: they carry no bytes and do not prove nonempty streaming, backpressure, cancellation, or failure timing.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "allOf": [
          {
            "oneOf": [
              {
                "properties": {
                  "bodyStream": {
                    "const": false
                  },
                  "contentLength": {
                    "const": 0
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "bodyStream",
                  "contentLength"
                ]
              },
              {
                "properties": {
                  "bodyStream": {
                    "const": true
                  },
                  "contentLength": {
                    "maximum": 104857600,
                    "minimum": 0,
                    "type": "integer"
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "bodyStream",
                  "contentLength"
                ]
              },
              {
                "properties": {
                  "bodyStream": {
                    "const": true
                  },
                  "contentLength": {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "bodyStream",
                  "contentLength"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "if": {
              "properties": {
                "method": {
                  "enum": [
                    "GET",
                    "HEAD"
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "then": {
              "properties": {
                "bodyStream": {
                  "const": false
                },
                "contentLength": {
                  "const": 0
                }
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "properties": {
          "bodyStream": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "contentLength": {
            "maximum": 104857600,
            "minimum": 0,
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "headers": {
            "default": [],
            "description": "Ordered header entries; repeated names are preserved in the Interface transport document. Content-Length (in any ASCII casing) is forbidden because contentLength alone frames the stream. Aggregate Latin-1 bytes are sum(len(name)+2+len(value)+2) and must not exceed 16384.",
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "name": {
                  "maxLength": 16380,
                  "minLength": 1,
                  "not": {
                    "pattern": "^[Cc][Oo][Nn][Tt][Ee][Nn][Tt]-[Ll][Ee][Nn][Gg][Tt][Hh]$"
                  },
                  "pattern": "^[!#$%&'*+\\-.^_`|~0-9A-Za-z]+$",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "value": {
                  "maxLength": 16379,
                  "pattern": "^[\\t\\x20-\\x7E\\x80-\\xFF]*$",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "name",
                "value"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            "maxItems": 64,
            "type": "array"
          },
          "method": {
            "enum": [
              "DELETE",
              "GET",
              "HEAD",
              "OPTIONS",
              "PATCH",
              "POST",
              "PUT"
            ],
            "type": "string"
          },
          "path": {
            "maxLength": 8192,
            "minLength": 1,
            "pattern": "^/([^/\\\\#\\x00-\\x20\\x7F-\\x9F][^\\\\#\\x00-\\x20\\x7F-\\x9F]*|)$",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "bodyStream",
          "contentLength",
          "method",
          "path"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "allOf": [
          {
            "oneOf": [
              {
                "properties": {
                  "bodyStream": {
                    "const": false
                  },
                  "contentLength": {
                    "const": 0
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "bodyStream",
                  "contentLength"
                ]
              },
              {
                "properties": {
                  "bodyStream": {
                    "const": true
                  },
                  "contentLength": {
                    "maximum": 104857600,
                    "minimum": 0,
                    "type": "integer"
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "bodyStream",
                  "contentLength"
                ]
              },
              {
                "properties": {
                  "bodyStream": {
                    "const": true
                  },
                  "contentLength": {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "bodyStream",
                  "contentLength"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "if": {
              "properties": {
                "status": {
                  "enum": [
                    204,
                    205,
                    304
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "then": {
              "properties": {
                "bodyStream": {
                  "const": false
                },
                "contentLength": {
                  "const": 0
                }
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "properties": {
          "bodyStream": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "contentLength": {
            "maximum": 104857600,
            "minimum": 0,
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "headers": {
            "default": [],
            "description": "Ordered header entries; repeated names are preserved in the Interface transport document. Content-Length (in any ASCII casing) is forbidden because contentLength alone frames the stream. Aggregate Latin-1 bytes are sum(len(name)+2+len(value)+2) and must not exceed 16384.",
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "name": {
                  "maxLength": 16380,
                  "minLength": 1,
                  "not": {
                    "pattern": "^[Cc][Oo][Nn][Tt][Ee][Nn][Tt]-[Ll][Ee][Nn][Gg][Tt][Hh]$"
                  },
                  "pattern": "^[!#$%&'*+\\-.^_`|~0-9A-Za-z]+$",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "value": {
                  "maxLength": 16379,
                  "pattern": "^[\\t\\x20-\\x7E\\x80-\\xFF]*$",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "name",
                "value"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            },
            "maxItems": 64,
            "type": "array"
          },
          "status": {
            "maximum": 599,
            "minimum": 200,
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "bodyStream",
          "contentLength",
          "status"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      "errors": [
        "backend_unavailable",
        "request_aborted",
        "request_too_large",
        "invalid_request",
        "response_aborted",
        "response_too_large"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "semantics": {
    "consistency": "per_key_linearizable"
  },
  "fixtures": [
    {
      "name": "get-without-body",
      "steps": [
        {
          "operation": "fetch",
          "input": {
            "bodyStream": false,
            "contentLength": 0,
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/healthz"
          },
          "expected": {
            "bodyStream": true,
            "contentLength": 0,
            "status": 200
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "repeated-header-metadata",
      "steps": [
        {
          "operation": "fetch",
          "input": {
            "bodyStream": true,
            "contentLength": null,
            "headers": [
              {
                "name": "X-Echo",
                "value": "a"
              },
              {
                "name": "X-Echo",
                "value": "b"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "path": "/echo"
          },
          "expected": {
            "bodyStream": true,
            "contentLength": 0,
            "headers": [
              {
                "name": "Set-Cookie",
                "value": "a=b"
              },
              {
                "name": "Set-Cookie",
                "value": "c=d"
              }
            ],
            "status": 200
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "head-response-has-no-body",
      "steps": [
        {
          "operation": "fetch",
          "input": {
            "bodyStream": false,
            "contentLength": 0,
            "method": "HEAD",
            "path": "/healthz"
          },
          "expected": {
            "bodyStream": false,
            "contentLength": 0,
            "status": 200
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "application-error-is-response",
      "steps": [
        {
          "operation": "fetch",
          "input": {
            "bodyStream": false,
            "contentLength": 0,
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/missing"
          },
          "expected": {
            "bodyStream": true,
            "contentLength": 0,
            "status": 404
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "unavailable-before-response-head",
      "steps": [
        {
          "operation": "fetch",
          "input": {
            "bodyStream": false,
            "contentLength": 0,
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/close-before-head"
          },
          "expectedError": "backend_unavailable"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

binding.definitionJson:
{
  "apiVersion": "bindings.takoform.com/v1alpha2",
  "kind": "BindingDefinition",
  "name": "module-worker.container-http",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "title": "Module Worker container HTTP binding",
  "description": "Unpublished module-worker.container-http Binding projecting the exact container.http fetch operation into a Worker Version under one JavaScript identifier. Runtime surface: env.NAME.fetch(request) returns a Promise<Response>; the request and response bodies stream with backpressure and cancellation, and the Promise resolves at response head. The Interface transport documents carry ordered entries, but the JavaScript Fetch projection uses standard Headers normalization: arbitrary duplicate fields may combine and their order/casing are not promised, while Set-Cookie remains separate through getSetCookie(). The target is only the authorized logical ContainerService UID and incarnation; URL hosts, native IDs, credentials, provider endpoints, and process authority are never exposed. Host and hop-by-hop headers are removed while application Authorization remains end-to-end. The transport document forbids application Content-Length because contentLength is its sole framing authority. At the Fetch boundary, the Binding extracts one canonical non-negative decimal Content-Length from an incoming request and removes it from projected application headers; duplicate, comma-joined, conflicting, or invalid framing yields invalid_request before dispatch, and a delivered-count mismatch yields request_aborted. Without a known exact length, contentLength is null. If the response head arrived early, abort the upload and any still-open response stream without replacing delivered status or bytes, or retrying. Native response Content-Length is transport-only: the Host validates and removes it before projection; duplicate, conflicting, or invalid framing fails pre-head as backend_unavailable. A known response above 104857600 bytes is response_too_large before its head, unknown overflow is the same body error after the head, and a response count mismatch aborts the exposed body as response_aborted. Before response head, backend_unavailable, request_aborted, request_too_large, response_too_large, and invalid_request reject; after response head, response_aborted and response_too_large are errored response-body outcomes. Application 4xx/5xx statuses resolve normally. There is no transparent retry after uncertain I/O, and existing calls stay pinned through the fixed 30000ms drain bound. This Binding is a local candidate only and does not imply Actor, WebSocket, stable API, Host support, or publication.",
  "sourceRole": "revision",
  "targetInterface": {
    "apiVersion": "interfaces.takoform.com/v1alpha1",
    "name": "container.http",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "schemaDigest": "sha256:65039b3ea0223057e5f34eff182098a1ba097ee351e19fcb7626a9af41a8561a"
  },
  "allowedTargetForms": [
    {
      "apiVersion": "edge.forms.takoform.com",
      "kind": "ContainerService"
    }
  ],
  "bindingNameGrammar": "^[A-Za-z_$][A-Za-z0-9_$]*$",
  "runtimeProjection": {
    "operations": [
      "fetch"
    ]
  },
  "lifecycle": {
    "targetDeletion": "refuse_while_bound"
  }
}

